00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:05.830
Where did I put it?

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:06.520
What file?

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:07.360
Like, what folder?

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:08.140
Did I delete it?

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:08.680
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.800
That's like, that's scary.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:13.180
You know, why can't
I find this function?

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.610
You know, you start spiraling,
you know, what did I do?

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.920
Did I save it in a
notepad or markdown?

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:20.220
Did I print it out and
then fax it to myself

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:23.510
like, you're going you're
going South, you know?

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.933
You know, I'll just
rewrite the function.

00:03:26.933 --> 00:03:28.350
You know, it takes
you 30 minutes,

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.250
an hour or two hours
again to rewrite it.

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:32.670
And so this is the
idea of packaging

00:03:32.670 --> 00:03:35.120
your code is that you want
to take those functions,

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:37.620
package them up so that they're
already in your R environment,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.828
and then you can just load
them up and then use them,

00:03:39.828 --> 00:03:41.790
and then also to
allow your coworkers

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:43.390
